s something to help me out.\n\n**Answer:** {"cards": ["♣A"]}\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation:\nThe situation is critical. The Next Player (Right) has only 1 card left and has just played a Jack (♦J).\n1.  **Pass**: If I pass, the Next Player wins the trick. Being the winner of the trick, they will lead their final card. If the Previous Player cannot or does not beat that final card, the Next Player wins the game immediately. I cannot risk this.\n2.  **Play ♣Q**: This beats the Jack. However, if the Next Player\'s last card is a King (K) or Ace (A), they can beat my Queen and win the game instantly. Since Kings are unaccounted for, this is a high-risk move.\n3.  **Play ♣A**: This beats the Jack and is the highest non-2/Joker single card. It blocks the Next Player if they are holding a King or Queen. While it breaks my pair of Aces, preventing the Next Player from going out is the top priority. If the Next Player holds a 2 or Joker, I will lose regardless, but playing the Ace covers the scenario where they hold a King.\n\nReason:\nI must win the trick to stop the Next Player (who has 1 card left) from going out. Passing guarantees a loss if the Previous Player doesn\'t intervene. Playing the Queen leaves me vulnerable to a King. Playing the Ace is the safest valid move to block the Next Player and attempt to regain the lead to play my remaining cards (QQ, A, 9).\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣A"]}'}
